[issue.1511]
number = 1511
title = "[P2] Restore PAY2's standalone lockfile for its declared locked qualification gates"
revision = "210639d0360c53f5c2fdd81c9c7c5e84b24b8c84"
verdict = "task"
evidence = "Commit a9a72229033ad1ff9513a28c686c6e6b6537d376 deleted services/agent/qualification/pay2/Cargo.lock, which remains absent despite the standalone workspace at services/agent/qualification/pay2/Cargo.toml:8, its ignore rule at services/agent/qualification/pay2/.gitignore:1 and the unchanged locked gates introduced by cbecc219e90f3e467ae5e393b631eec43bb6a696 and retained in the done task at spec/layerx-merge/spec.kvx:131523 and spec/layerx-merge/spec.kvx:131536; services/agent/qualification/pay2/build.rs:10 only reads retained sources, services/agent/qualification/pay2/tests/build_inputs.rs:7 checks those inputs, and services/agent/qualification/pay2/pay2e_test.rs:316 and services/agent/qualification/pay2/pay2e_test.rs:356 retain node readiness without registering the funded test as a Cargo target."
close_comment = "PAY2 still needs its tracked standalone lockfile and a matching ignore policy to reproduce the declared locked compilation gates from a fresh checkout. The repair is specified with regression coverage while preserving node readiness; test compilation alone does not establish funded PAY2 execution."

